Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:21:14 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Browse Trips + Trip Detail: fix off-brand hardcoded colors,
 add trust banner

Browse Trips / trip-card:
- Header and pagination were hardcoded to the old green (#1E7A50) and to
  Tailwind's stock blue/purple, bypassing the token system entirely --
  fixed to use brand/accent tokens.
- Trip card's photo-less fallback gradient and the Quick Trip "Show
  Interest" button were similarly hardcoded (purple-600, orange-500) --
  fixed to brand tokens.
- Dropped the green heart emoji on "Free Trip" badges, which visually
  clashed against the brand-coral label text next to it.
- Left the per-province badge colors and Quick Trip urgency/countdown
  styling (orange) alone -- those are deliberate semantic/categorical
  color choices, not brand-hue bugs.
- Updated the Browse Trips header subhead to name the three launch route
  clusters instead of generic "amazing travel opportunities" copy.

Trip Detail:
- Added the trust banner from the redesign brief ("Fellow traveller, not
  a verified companion. You're responsible for arrangements and safety.")
  above the organizer info -- this didn't exist on the page before. The
  locked-chat / interest-request flow underneath it was already accurate
  and didn't need changing.
- Fixed the same hardcoded purple-600 fallback-image gradient as trip-card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
